message.content:
This appears to be a CBP ruling on diamond painting keychain kits. These are sets put up for retail sale, and GRI 3(b) requires classifying by the component that gives the set its essential character. The decorative plastic charm is the main component, which the consumer embellishes with crystal diamonds. Candidate headings are 3926 (other articles of plastics), 7117 (imitation jewelry), and 4421.

The most likely classification is 3926.40.0090 (statuettes and other ornamental articles, of plastics). However, keychain charms could be classed under 3926.40 as ornamental articles. Key rings with charms fall under 7117 (imitation jewelry) only if they are finished articles; here the plastic piece is decorated with crystal diamonds, which are glass or plastic beads. The kit is a craft kit, and I recall CBP rulings classifying similar diamond painting keychain kits in 3926.40.0090.

{"hts_code": "3926.40.0090", "reason": "The kits are sets under GRI 3(b), with the decorative plastic charm piece giving the essential character, so they are classified as other ornamental articles of plastics."}
